A||||2||Vlad||How to check ball joint.||||5||
Z||000000||Vlad||01-07-2001||09:12 AM||||Hello<P>I have a 6-12 slop in both front wheels (85 GT). Point of thinking is either ball joints or bearings.<P>How do I check ball joints for proper operation with removed wheel.<P>Thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||Will||01-07-2001||09:29 AM||||It's actually easier to check for play with the wheel on. The diameter of the wheel gives you more leverage on the ball joint.<BR>The best thing to do is have a helper (no easy way to do it without one) lie under the car and observe the suspension as you do the 6-12 shake. The helper should look for three things: movement of the steering knuckle relative to the lower control arm (bad lower ball joint), movement of the steering knuckle relative to the upper control arm (bad upper ball joint), and movement of the wheel and brake rotor relative to the steering knuckle (wheel bearing needs adjustment/replacement). The motion is going to be very small, less than 1/16 inch. If you find the upper ball joint on one side is bad, the upper on the other side is not far behind it; same goes for lowers. All four ball joints can be had from Autozone, with a lifetime guarantee (free balljoints forever!), for about $75.<BR>I haven't had to buy new bearing yet, but wheel bearing adjustment procedures are in the shop manual, which you should have if you do any serious work to the car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Vlad||01-07-2001||09:45 AM||||Thank you Will. Great help.<P>The problem is that I have already had such a slop in both front wheels and it was gone for a while after bearings adjustment. <BR>However, here it is again. I can guess I was afraid to overtiten bearings and didn't snag them good enough. I don't have a torque wrench. Don't know.......( <BR>Bearings themselves seemed to be in very good shape.<BR>Well.... Going to take a closer look today. <BR>Hope it will be bearings again.<BR>I just don't want to start messing with ball joints now since I'm planning to take control arms off and make them have Poly bushings as part of preparations for new Solo2 season.<P>Thanks again||||reg||1
